      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Alternatives: Bullet Unity, Havok Unity or maybe even allow people to make physics using the built-in Unity PhysX based system which are all GPU accelerated - VRC is heavy on the CPU anyway so outsourcing stuff to the GPU would work.\n\nAlso, in some ways, the holy grail is to allow animation overrides that move non-humanoid bones. Currently VRC doesn't allow for this. You know how most games *manually* animate the skirt, long hair, etc. during for example running animations? This is both extremely performant *and* can look as good as you want *and* helps keep the \"creative ceiling\" of VRC avatars high. As of right now though... it doesn't work, VRC doesn't support it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5c3828b8fb6e24014246a11d",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5ab16fb14c0c3b511e9a4d9b",
        "alias": "Fun Orangutan",
        "aliasID": "65c3d44eed6eefce4c35fd71",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/5cd57ec4f1f6e0a53310c2f0d06fceb5.jpg",
        "created": "2018-03-20T20:31:45.659Z",
        "name": "Maribel Hearn",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2019-01-11T05:25:12.300Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5c2ac37d3727342de8f41e21",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Dynamic bones don't eat frames as much as they want you to believe. \n\nThe biggest eater of frames is the lack of multi-threading.\nThe second biggest is IK, based on everything I have heard from so many people.\nAnother great place to start would be to reduce the performance impact of name plates.\n\nIf the game was multithreaded, people could have 1000 dynamic bone transforms on them and there could be 50 players in the room and you could still be at 45 FPS or better, assuming you are running a fairly recent i7 quad core or better CPU (A rough guess based on the CPU usage VRChat currently displays.)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
